   "src": "Item 229 (Justin 2026-10-19: \"a really high pitched whistling in the music that is kinda irritating\"), measured: the title has a steady 14.07 kHz tone (-64 dBFS, 23 dB over its neighbours), notched 28 dB; the Dungeon ambience carries a comb of pure tones at every 200 Hz from 3.6 to 12 kHz (up to 27 dB over its neighbours), so it takes a 24 dB per octave low-pass at 2.8 kHz (the tones 12 to 45 dB down, its drone below 2 kHz untouched). The other tracks have no audible tone. Item 253 (Justin 2026-10-20: \"lots of high pirched chirping in water plane music if we could filter out\"), measured by bursts (third-octave bands, frames 12 dB over the band's median): the Plane of Water's score chirps 2.4 to 4.6 kHz, about 82 bursts a minute, peaks -32 dB at 3.2 and 4 kHz against a -30 dB body, each a narrow tone that sweeps, so a broad cut, not a notch: peaking 3.6 kHz, Q 1.1, -14 dB takes the chirps' peaks 12 to 13 dB down at 3.2 and 4 kHz and 9 dB at 2.5 kHz, the body (100 Hz to 2 kHz) unchanged. Of the other planes, Fire has dense broadband crackle bursts rising to 16 kHz (likely its own fire), Earth mild bursts at 2.5 kHz with its notes, Air, Light and Shadow none; none filtered."
  },
  "src": "A11 (1.7 musicEnds, playMusic): a song whose last half second is silent rests 5 s between plays. A13 (1.7 audioRetryDelay): a failed track is asked for again after 5 s, doubling to 30 s. A12 (1.7 AUDIO_MUSIC_LRU, 2026-10-14): a tablet keeps one decoded track, a desktop three."
